title: Tutorial — How This Works
authors: Writing Journals tutorial, built in lo-blocks
description: Professor Ellington spends two minutes showing the student how the tool works — the conversation advances on Continue, activities land in the right pane, work saves as you type, and the tabs collect everything — then sends them to the Writers' Circle for their first journal.
~~~~

How This Works
--------------
Ellington: before I hand you over to your first journal, give me two minutes to show you how this thing works. [face=calm]

Ellington: this left side is a conversation. it moves when you click **Continue** below — which you've apparently already worked out. [face=smile]

tut_sidebar <- tut_welcome

Ellington: the right side is where the work happens. read the card that just landed, then click **Mark as read** at the bottom of it — **Continue** stays off until you do. it's over there ---> [face=explaining]

--- wait @tut_welcome_done.value ---

Try It Once
-----------
tut_sidebar <- tut_practice

Ellington: good. now the other half. when there's something to *do*, it shows up on the right the same way — and the box should be trying to get your attention right now. [face=explaining]

Ellington: type anything at all in it. one word is plenty. [face=smile]

--- wait @tut_practice_text.value ---

Ellington: notice you never clicked "save" — there is no save button anywhere in here. every keystroke is kept as you go. you could close this tab mid-sentence and your half-sentence would be waiting when you came back. [face=calm]

The Tabs
--------
tut_sidebar <- tut_tabs_note

Ellington: last thing. the tabs along the top collect everything in one place — in the journals that's your running work, the people you're talking to, and the page where you export a PDF to hand in at the end. [face=explaining]

Ellington: the conversation will point you to a tab whenever it matters, and you can always come back — nothing locks behind you. try the **Tips** tab up top if you're curious, then come back to **Main Content**. [face=smile]

That's Everything
-----------------
tut_sidebar <- tut_finish

Ellington: that's the whole machine. conversation on the left, work on the right, tabs up top. [face=smile]

Ellington: your first journal is called "Who Am I As a Writer?" — three students who call themselves the Writers' Circle are expecting you. tap **Continue** and I'll take you over. [face=calm]

--- pause ---

wj_course.selectedChild <- edu.memphis.writing.sba/wj1_sba_part1
